From 14799c779c9ff767e99ebfaebd9af87b05b74882 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 05:46:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: let the test suite build and log in again

The tests had fallen behind the plug-in, and `tests` no longer linked.

The webOS patches call libpurple functions the test mock does not
have (purple_signal_emit, purple_timeout_add,
purple_blist_node_set_bool, purple_get_core,
purple_accounts_get_handle). They also call the webOS call service in
call-luna.cpp, which the tests do not build. Add the functions to the
mock. Stub the call service, which needs a bus the tests do not have.
purple_timeout_add runs its function once, at once, so the delayed
receipt frees what it holds.

Every test also starts with a login that no longer matched the
plug-in. TDLib's database is now in
/media/cryptofs/.purple-tdlib-db/<number>, not under
purple_user_dir(). Since "Honour "Keep inline downloads" again,
through use_storage_optimizer", a setOption request follows
setTdlibParameters. Expect both, with the option off when
keep-inline-downloads is set.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
